1) [done] triangulations. make them robust, with incircle tests and refinement

2) [done] sphere groups, possibly with orbifold -- wraps GAP's own SphereGroup
   (see src/sphere.jl for why: Knuth-Bendix normal forms, intersection
   numbers, and automorphism-group computation are deep enough that
   reimplementing them natively isn't worthwhile; requires the "img" GAP
   package to be loadable, see src/sphere.jl header for setup)

3) marked triangulations

4) rational maps, recorded by critical points and values (rather than coefficients), and normalization. (in degree 1, misses 3 params; in degree 2, misses 1 param. in degree >=3, probably ok).
- conversion to classical format
- equations that enforce the points to be consistent
- compute preimages of points in this model, test intersection between curve (arc of great circle) and curve.
